From a75010ce97eeb5a252d3a58eb1d4f2edc8b47559 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: small-gear-lab <289302950+marie-222@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:02:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Draw images over the area of a Neovim window

neovide.image_set takes the handle of a Neovim window and a map of options
(path, path2, mode, zoom, actual, x, y, opacity, split, gain, background);
neovide.image_clear removes the image. The image is decoded with the image
crate (PNG, JPEG, WebP, GIF, BMP, ICO) and drawn with Skia into the pixel
region of the window's grid, above the text and below floating windows.
Modes: single, difference, blend and swipe, for comparing two images.
Each rendered window remembers the handle of its Neovim window.
